WEBVTT

00:01.100 --> 00:04.645
"It seems today that all you see

00:04.770 --> 00:08.190
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:08.190 --> 00:11.945
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:12.069 --> 00:14.154
"On which we used to rely?

00:14.864 --> 00:18.200
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.325 --> 00:23.205
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:23.330 --> 00:24.790
"Laugh and cry

00:24.873 --> 00:30.295
"He's a family guy

00:33.131 --> 00:36.342
On the whole, I enjoy my job as a pharmacist.

00:36.467 --> 00:40.013
In fact, many of my customers
are your mommies and daddies.

00:40.096 --> 00:44.475
Jimmy, your mother had awful postpartum
depression after you were born.

00:44.600 --> 00:50.314
And, Danielle, your father had very bad
haemorrhoids that stung him unmerciful.

00:50.314 --> 00:54.903
They were awful. They were like
stinky little balloons. Ugh!

00:55.028 --> 00:57.404
I gave him some special ointment,

00:57.529 --> 01:02.118
and he hurt so bad that he had to
apply it in the car with his sock.

01:03.369 --> 01:04.494
Thank you.

01:04.620 --> 01:06.997
- Cool! I wanna be a pharmacist!
- Yeah!

01:07.122 --> 01:10.876
Thank you, Mr Goldman.
Our final speaker is Mr Griffin.

01:10.959 --> 01:14.212
- Yeah!
- Hey, kids! You know what I do?

01:14.295 --> 01:17.425
I work at a toy factory.
And you know what I do there?

01:17.549 --> 01:20.344
I bet you're just a low-level
assembly-line guy

01:20.469 --> 01:22.971
who stands all day
screwing heads on dolls.

01:23.054 --> 01:27.017
"Ooh, is it on straight?"
"I don't know. " Boo!

01:27.850 --> 01:30.062
- Why, you snot-nosed...
- Mr Griffin!

01:30.145 --> 01:32.439
He plays in the park. Get him there.

01:32.439 --> 01:34.733
Does anyone have any questions?

01:34.858 --> 01:37.443
Can we listen to the claims adjuster again?

01:37.568 --> 01:40.696
Yeah!

01:42.782 --> 01:44.866
Welcome back to Quahog Five News.

01:44.950 --> 01:48.287
Here's Ollie Williams with
the "Black You" weather forecast.

01:48.412 --> 01:50.372
- It's gonna rain!
- Thanks, Ollie.

01:50.497 --> 01:53.417
Finally, we go to Asian reporter
Tricia Takanawa,

01:53.501 --> 01:56.546
interviewing a guy
from the Renaissance Fair.

01:56.629 --> 02:00.591
Thanks, Tom. Sir, for those who
aren't familiar with the tradition,

02:00.591 --> 02:03.009
tell us about the Renaissance Fair.

02:03.092 --> 02:05.387
Yea. But first, bride of Genghis,

02:05.512 --> 02:09.683
thou must explainest to me
thy very peculiar electronic wand.

02:09.766 --> 02:11.768
Whoooooo!

02:11.852 --> 02:14.771
Rupert, are you ready to hear our "mad lib"?

02:14.896 --> 02:19.150
Ahem. "Cinderella had three
wicked step-watermelons

02:19.275 --> 02:21.778
who were very smelly to her. "

02:21.861 --> 02:26.783
"So her fairy god-toilet turned
a pumpkin into a fanny

02:26.867 --> 02:28.951
and sent her off to the poop. "

02:30.203 --> 02:33.330
Oh, my! How ruthlessly absurd.

02:33.455 --> 02:36.374
Peter, how was your presentation
to Chris's class?

02:36.458 --> 02:39.712
- It was a waste of time.
- It couldn't have been that bad.

02:39.796 --> 02:44.800
I was terrible. Everyone else had an important
job and was way more successful than me.

02:44.925 --> 02:47.929
Come on. You... You have a great job.

02:48.054 --> 02:51.890
Yeah. You're... you're doing...
you're doing good.

02:52.016 --> 02:55.143
If you're not satisfied,
then be more assertive.

02:55.227 --> 02:58.771
Invite Mr Weed to dinner
and show him what you have to offer.

02:58.897 --> 03:01.274
I guess I could. I just hope it goes OK.

03:01.274 --> 03:04.736
We've had bad luck with guests.
Remember Margot Kidder?

03:04.820 --> 03:09.407
We loved you in the Superman movies.
You were just wonderful.

03:10.034 --> 03:12.118
Aaghhh!

03:21.919 --> 03:24.214
Mr Weed, I, uh... was wondering

03:24.338 --> 03:27.967
if maybe you'd like to come to
my house for dinner Friday night.

03:27.967 --> 03:30.386
- That wasn't so hard.
- What time?

03:30.469 --> 03:33.723
- 7.30, 8.00?
- Fabulous! What shall I bring?

03:35.057 --> 03:37.350
Calm down. Everything will be fine.

03:37.475 --> 03:41.729
If I blow this, I'll have to go back to
my old job at The Electric Company.

03:41.855 --> 03:44.024
- Duh...
- Ot.

03:44.149 --> 03:46.026
Dot.

03:46.109 --> 03:47.986
- Buh...
- Et.

03:48.112 --> 03:50.072
- Bet.
- Bet. I knew that. Slow down.

03:50.197 --> 03:52.157
- Puh...
- It.

03:52.157 --> 03:54.242
- Pit.
- Pit. Come on, it's my first day.

03:54.368 --> 03:56.036
- Fuh...
- At.

03:56.119 --> 03:57.996
- Fat.
- Oh, that's it, buddy!

04:00.624 --> 04:02.792
That must be him.

04:02.792 --> 04:07.381
Oh, God. I hope I don't get so nervous
I can't control the volume of my voice.

04:07.506 --> 04:09.257
Hello, Peter. How are you?

04:09.382 --> 04:11.676
Fine! Please come in.

04:12.384 --> 04:14.679
It's so nice to have you over, Mr Weed.

04:14.804 --> 04:18.641
Thank you, Mrs Griffin. I understand
you have a beautiful family.

04:18.766 --> 04:22.812
We do. But the children won't be
joining us for dinner. It's their bedtime.

04:27.608 --> 04:29.694
- State your names.
- Meg!

04:29.818 --> 04:31.987
- Chris!
- And I'm Liesl.

04:32.112 --> 04:35.532
The Griffin children would like
to say good night to you.

06:00.198 --> 06:03.326
Mmmm. Who would think that
a woman with such beauty

06:03.451 --> 06:06.245
would have the culinary skills
of Emeril Lagasse?

06:06.245 --> 06:08.539
Well, thank you.

06:08.665 --> 06:10.332
Bam!

06:11.249 --> 06:14.920
Ahem. Peter, don't you have
something to say to Mr Weed?

06:15.003 --> 06:16.463
Oh, yeah.

06:16.588 --> 06:21.593
Mr Weed, I don't care what the guys at work
say. I don't think you're an effeminate weirdo.

06:21.677 --> 06:24.096
Uh, so, what kind of a name is "Weed"?

06:24.179 --> 06:26.682
They gave it to my grandfather
on Ellis Island.

06:26.682 --> 06:29.183
Our original name was Bermuda Grass.

06:29.308 --> 06:33.354
Peter, being here with your wonderful
family, your beautiful home

06:33.479 --> 06:37.108
and your funny talking dog...
well, I'm impressed.

06:37.233 --> 06:41.070
Starting Monday, I'd like to promote you
to head of toy development.

06:41.695 --> 06:45.366
Holy crap! Oh, thanks, Mr Weed!
You won't be sorry.

06:45.449 --> 06:48.161
Brian, quit it. You're embarrassing me.

06:48.286 --> 06:51.413
Brian's choking!
Do the Heimlich manoeuvre, quick!

06:58.171 --> 06:59.838
He's dead.

06:59.963 --> 07:02.049
Aaagh! Aaagh!

07:03.300 --> 07:06.012
I forgot my purse. Aaaghhh!

07:08.179 --> 07:11.516
Let's not panic.
Nobody even knows about this yet.

07:11.516 --> 07:13.810
Police! Random dead-body search!

07:13.935 --> 07:16.939
- Oh, my God! Stall 'em!
- Peter, what are you doing?

07:17.564 --> 07:19.566
Just stall 'em, Lois!

07:22.569 --> 07:26.030
Ha-ha! Gotcha! It's just me - Death.
I'm here for the body.

07:26.114 --> 07:28.825
Ah. Peter, it's OK. It's just Death.

07:28.825 --> 07:30.409
Ah, thank God.

07:30.493 --> 07:34.163
- Did someone choke on a roll in here?
- No, no, no. I spit it up.

07:34.247 --> 07:35.498
Oh.

07:36.123 --> 07:39.169
Our top story:
Doreen, I lost your phone number.

07:39.252 --> 07:41.754
We met at the Sky Lounge
last night. Call me.

07:41.879 --> 07:45.716
In other news, toy industrialist
Jonathan Weed was found dead

07:45.716 --> 07:49.262
in the home of an employee
who claims Weed choked on a roll.

07:49.262 --> 07:53.766
No charges will be filed against
the employee, but the roll is in custody.

08:00.522 --> 08:03.776
I'd do her, do her, wouldn't do her.

08:03.858 --> 08:06.153
Ech, who hasn't done her? Do her.

08:06.278 --> 08:09.489
Lose the pigtails and we'll talk.
Do her, do her...

08:09.489 --> 08:14.911
And now, the last man to see Jonathan Weed
alive has offered to say a few words.

08:15.036 --> 08:16.288
Good afternoon.

08:16.371 --> 08:21.293
As you know, we of the Christian faith
believe that Jesus is not really dead,

08:21.376 --> 08:24.087
but that he must let
the world think he is dead

08:24.212 --> 08:29.926
until he can find a way to control
the raging spirit that dwells within him.

08:35.973 --> 08:40.352
Anyway, before he died, Mr Weed
promoted me to head of toy development.

08:40.352 --> 08:44.649
I brought my attorney who confirms
that this constitutes a verbal contract.

08:44.732 --> 08:49.111
Isn't that right, Saul?
"Yes, sir. " Thank you.

08:50.488 --> 08:53.073
Glad you all found your way
from the cemetery.

08:53.073 --> 08:57.869
I'm Mr Weed's lawyer. We found this tape
among Mr Weed's personal effects

08:57.869 --> 09:02.582
with instructions that it be screened
immediately after his funeral. Enjoy.

09:02.665 --> 09:04.668
Good morning. Camera time.

09:04.752 --> 09:09.463
- Turn that off. I don't have my face on yet.
- You want to tell us what you're making?

09:09.547 --> 09:13.718
It's just a couple of eggs with
the peppers left over from last night.

09:13.842 --> 09:15.303
- Mm...
- Yes.

09:15.387 --> 09:18.097
OK, playtime is over.
Turn it off, monkey, OK?

09:18.222 --> 09:20.808
Ahem.

09:20.934 --> 09:25.813
Hello, friends. If you are watching this,
I am dead, and I bet you're pretty bummed.

09:25.938 --> 09:27.689
- But I have good news.
- Yeah?

09:27.814 --> 09:30.735
The Happy-Go-Lucky Toy Factory
shall be torn down

09:30.819 --> 09:34.488
to make way for the Happy-Go-Lucky
Terminal Disease Institute.

09:34.572 --> 09:37.700
- What?!
- The demolition will begin in... now.

09:42.705 --> 09:44.790
OK, we've got your typing test here

09:44.915 --> 09:48.127
and all the pertinent data
about your, um...

09:48.127 --> 09:50.421
um, you know, your background

09:50.546 --> 09:55.217
and, um... skills and...

09:56.176 --> 09:58.553
- And?
- I gotta be honest with you.

09:58.679 --> 10:03.266
I only have another week and a half here,
and I have completely checked out.

10:03.349 --> 10:06.061
- Oh.
- Yeah.

10:06.602 --> 10:08.563
Well, what should I do?

10:08.563 --> 10:10.440
Um...

10:12.651 --> 10:14.527
Chef?

10:21.075 --> 10:24.328
Sorry, we're out of towels.
Let me get that for you, sir.

10:42.262 --> 10:46.641
I should pay two bucks for stickers
cos this guy can't hear? Come on!

10:46.725 --> 10:49.645
Hey, I might be deaf, but I have feelings!

10:49.645 --> 10:53.315
Oh, uh... I mean, what?

10:53.398 --> 10:58.111
- Has Dad found a permanent job yet?
- He's going through a career transition.

10:58.194 --> 11:02.783
He's sampling a few things, searching
for something that fits him just right.

11:04.367 --> 11:08.413
- Clearly it's not that tube top.
- Looking for a good time, sweet cheeks?

11:08.538 --> 11:11.666
- Oh, my God.
- Peter, get in the car!

11:11.749 --> 11:14.669
OK, but it'll cost ya.
You want a Cleveland Steamer?

11:14.794 --> 11:17.504
Get in the car...
What's a Cleveland Steamer?

11:17.588 --> 11:20.091
- It means he'll...
- Whoa, be cool.

11:20.091 --> 11:25.095
Yes, you go to Maple Street,
and then take a left, and then you go...

11:25.220 --> 11:27.932
- So you want to party or what?
- Get in right now!

11:31.059 --> 11:34.395
It's eerie, isn't it?
Like looking into the future.

11:35.730 --> 11:39.818
- Forgetful Freddy was so forgetful...
- How forgetful?

11:39.901 --> 11:45.323
He was so forgetful, whenever he tried
to remember a name, he drew a... "blank".

11:48.034 --> 11:52.538
This is all my fault. If I hadn't pushed you
so hard to invite Mr Weed to dinner,

11:52.621 --> 11:55.125
he'd still be alive and you'd have your job.

11:55.125 --> 11:58.795
We'll get through this.
We just have to scrimp a little.

11:58.878 --> 12:00.963
Sell some stuff we don't really need.

12:01.088 --> 12:04.216
- This'll bring in a couple of bucks.
- Peter, listen.

12:04.300 --> 12:09.012
When we got married, you always talked
about your dream job. Remember?

12:09.096 --> 12:12.434
You put that dream aside
in order to provide for this family.

12:12.559 --> 12:15.561
- Yeah.
- I've saved some money from teaching piano,

12:15.686 --> 12:19.105
and this is the perfect time
for you to pursue that dream.

12:19.231 --> 12:20.482
- Really?
- Yes!

12:20.566 --> 12:24.653
Wow. Since money's tight, I was gonna
suggest that we eat the kids.

12:24.736 --> 12:28.073
Jokingly at first, but then
I was gonna gauge your reaction.

12:28.198 --> 12:32.452
If you were cool with it, we could go
from there. But this is a much better idea!

12:32.577 --> 12:35.371
I'm gonna do it!
I'm gonna realise my dream!

12:35.496 --> 12:38.708
I am gonna be a Renaissance Fair jouster!

12:38.833 --> 12:40.585
Oh, Peter!

12:41.210 --> 12:43.004
Aaaghhh!

12:46.633 --> 12:49.969
This is so exciting!
My little jouster's first day.

12:50.095 --> 12:54.139
- Here's your lunch.
- Thanks, honey. Aw, egg salad!

12:54.265 --> 12:56.850
- Have a good time.
- I'll try.

12:59.478 --> 13:01.855
- Hey, Mort.
- Oh, God! Don't hurt me!

13:01.855 --> 13:04.775
- Oh, hi, Peter.
- You gonna be a jouster, too?

13:04.900 --> 13:07.903
Yes. I'm trying to overcome
my fear of swords

13:08.028 --> 13:11.865
because a man in a pirate suit
stabbed me in the ear when I was five,

13:11.990 --> 13:14.993
and then again when I was 30.
And you? The same?

13:15.119 --> 13:19.163
Nah, not really. It kinda
all goes back to when I was 18.

13:19.163 --> 13:23.877
I was going through that rebellious phase,
and I was hanging out with a bad crowd.

13:23.960 --> 13:27.296
Here, Peter. Try one of these.

13:27.421 --> 13:30.551
- What is it?
- It's a cheeseburger.

13:32.844 --> 13:34.930
Now I know it wasn't a cheeseburger.

13:35.013 --> 13:38.558
But at that time,
I was ready to believe anything.

13:40.018 --> 13:41.895
I didn't know what was going on.

13:41.895 --> 13:45.564
I wandered around and ended up
at the Renaissance Fair.

13:45.647 --> 13:48.693
- I can fly!
- Oh, my God!

13:52.029 --> 13:57.243
I was saved by the one and only Black
Knight of the Quahog Renaissance Fair.

13:57.327 --> 14:01.622
A word of advice. The path to knighthood
is paved with strength and nobility,

14:01.706 --> 14:04.208
not LSD and sideburns.

14:04.333 --> 14:09.964
And from that moment on, I knew
someday I wanted to be a knight like him.

14:10.047 --> 14:14.343
Mercy! I was once addicted
to antihistamines.

14:14.426 --> 14:17.345
I took so many, I thought I was Mr Peanut.

14:17.345 --> 14:19.432
Yeah, that's a great story, too.

14:19.556 --> 14:22.476
So, you think you got
what it takes to be jousters!

14:22.559 --> 14:26.438
If you're gonna joust, you gotta want it!
Let me hear your war cry!

14:28.190 --> 14:30.483
Is that the best you got, you pile of crap?

14:30.483 --> 14:34.570
Yes. From an early age,
my parents discouraged loud noises.

14:34.654 --> 14:36.948
You're a candy-ass maggot!

14:37.782 --> 14:40.075
- Something funny, maggot?
- No, sir!

14:40.201 --> 14:43.329
- You love the Middle Ages, don't you?
- Sir, yes, sir!

14:43.412 --> 14:47.583
The concept of a geocentric universe
gets you sexually excited, doesn't it?

14:47.708 --> 14:48.543
Yes, sir!

14:48.626 --> 14:53.130
You want to make 16th-century
mathematician Johannes Kepler your bitch?

14:53.214 --> 14:54.881
Sir, yes, sir!

14:55.006 --> 14:58.010
- Welcome, apprentices.
- It's him.

14:58.010 --> 15:03.974
Look alive. Allow me to introduce the best
of the best, the Black Knight himself!

15:04.057 --> 15:08.228
And this is his trophy wench,
Maid Madeleine.

15:14.817 --> 15:15.861
Ding!

15:20.031 --> 15:22.950
- Excuse me, Mr Black Knight.
- I'm busy.

15:23.034 --> 15:27.831
I just wanted to thank you. I don't know
if you remember, but when I was a kid,

15:27.831 --> 15:30.123
you helped me get my life back on track.

15:30.248 --> 15:33.461
Agh! Dammit! Look, I'm busy, all right?

15:33.586 --> 15:36.505
- OK, I'll come back later.
- Damn rookies.

15:36.589 --> 15:39.508
Are all the other men
out of the shower yet?

15:42.635 --> 15:47.432
Hey, porker. Yes, I'm calling you a porker,
and there's nothing you can do about it

15:47.557 --> 15:52.353
because I'm protected by my
impenetrable cereal-box fort. Ha-ha-ha!

15:52.437 --> 15:54.106
Hey, you! Drunkie.

15:54.231 --> 15:58.193
Yes, I'm calling you drunkie, and
there's nothing you can do about it...

15:58.277 --> 15:59.236
Agh!

15:59.945 --> 16:02.448
- The toast is ready.
- I'll get it, Lois.

16:06.200 --> 16:07.660
Here you go.

16:07.660 --> 16:10.579
Maybe you shouldn't bring
your lance to the table.

16:10.705 --> 16:15.376
If I'm gonna impress the Black Knight,
my lance must be with me at all times.

16:15.501 --> 16:18.504
You guys will be so proud
when you see me on that field.

16:18.629 --> 16:20.799
Excuse me. I gotta go practise.

16:21.341 --> 16:23.718
Oh, my God, Dad, my earring!

16:23.718 --> 16:26.428
Dad, stop! Argh!

16:28.305 --> 16:29.890
Two mutton joints, please.

16:29.974 --> 16:33.853
Oh, thou wishest to feast on
the appendage of a humble ovine.

16:33.936 --> 16:38.524
Listen, freak. We don't all watch Frasier.
Now give me two mutton joints.

16:39.357 --> 16:40.609
Thank you.

16:53.538 --> 16:56.875
'Tis a glorious afternoon.
Wouldst thou not agree?

16:56.875 --> 16:59.920
Uh, yea, kind shrew.

17:00.003 --> 17:05.217
Uh, I before thee... except after C.

17:05.217 --> 17:08.678
Wouldst thou take a gander
underneath my frock?

17:09.178 --> 17:11.889
Uh, sure. Whatever floats your boat.

17:14.934 --> 17:17.103
There you go.

17:17.228 --> 17:18.687
Frickin' perverts.

17:18.770 --> 17:21.690
Madeleine, go wait in the Hyundai!

17:21.690 --> 17:23.567
What were you doing with my girl?

17:23.692 --> 17:28.989
She walks over here and asks me to put a bird
in her panties! I'm going "What the hell?"

17:29.114 --> 17:32.951
Oh, God! Peter, play dead!
Curl up in an ass ball or something!

17:32.951 --> 17:35.872
- What's the problem, BK?
- I don't like you.

17:35.997 --> 17:38.916
And I don't like you hanging around my girl.

17:38.999 --> 17:41.418
I don't ever want to see you here again.

17:41.501 --> 17:45.589
Oh. OK, but we can see each other
outside the fair, right?

17:45.672 --> 17:49.758
- I'm just trying to understand the rules.
- If I see you again, I'll kill you!

17:49.843 --> 17:51.928
OK, that's much clearer.

17:52.554 --> 17:55.598
Oh, God! I think I just miscarried!

17:59.018 --> 18:02.772
What are you doing? I spent hours
soldering that costume for you.

18:02.772 --> 18:05.483
I don't need it any more. I quit the team.

18:05.608 --> 18:09.445
You can't quit jousting.
The big meet is today. I thought...

18:09.571 --> 18:12.990
Did you just say "big meat"?

18:14.033 --> 18:15.826
Oh, my God, I did.

18:17.995 --> 18:20.622
- We almost missed that.
- That was a close one.

18:20.706 --> 18:25.002
But I'm being serious here. We were
all set to come see you joust today.

18:25.085 --> 18:28.339
You were so excited to be
on the field with the Black Knight.

18:28.422 --> 18:30.841
I'll be watching him from the stands,

18:30.924 --> 18:35.720
because the Black Knight is a big jerk,
just like that guy who fixed our vacuum.

18:35.846 --> 18:37.805
There you go. All fixed.

18:37.930 --> 18:40.725
A half-eaten meatball was
clogging up the intake.

18:40.851 --> 18:45.313
- Oh. Well, did you save it?
- Uh, no.

18:45.438 --> 18:46.772
You bastard.

18:50.442 --> 18:55.030
It's an exciting day here at
the Renaissance Fair, wouldn't you say, Tom?

18:55.113 --> 18:59.077
It would be if you didn't remind us all
of our grandmother's cleavage.

18:59.201 --> 19:03.580
Let's go to the field, where the Black Knight
prepares to challenge his opponent.

19:13.048 --> 19:15.759
"Ohh...

19:15.884 --> 19:17.010
"Hey

19:17.135 --> 19:20.890
"Ohh...

19:20.972 --> 19:22.140
"Hey

19:22.849 --> 19:27.020
Hey, how you doing there, big guy?

19:27.854 --> 19:29.939
You holding up all right?

19:31.107 --> 19:34.652
You want a soda? Hm?

19:35.569 --> 19:37.029
Oh, screw it. I tried.

19:37.156 --> 19:40.366
The Black Knight's next challenger
is Sir Mort Goldman.

19:50.376 --> 19:52.462
Oh, God! I forfeit!

19:52.587 --> 19:57.466
That's it. The Black Knight is out of
challengers and is once again undefeated.

19:57.591 --> 19:59.969
Hey, what's your fat ass doing here?

19:59.969 --> 20:02.471
He's my only means of conveyance.

20:02.596 --> 20:05.390
- But I guess I do spoil him.
- Clearly you do.

20:05.515 --> 20:10.103
And what are you doing here, Griffin?
I told you never to come here again!

20:10.186 --> 20:14.274
- I don't want any trouble.
- You've got trouble if you don't beat it.

20:14.357 --> 20:17.069
- Listen, buddy...
- I said get lost!

20:18.528 --> 20:21.448
- Where's he going?
- Let him go, kids.

20:21.573 --> 20:24.993
You see that, kids?
Your father's nothing but a fizzle!

20:25.118 --> 20:27.912
Nobody calls me a fizzle
and gets away with it!

20:30.207 --> 20:34.378
Except that guy who called me a fizzle
and then ran off. He got away with it.

20:34.503 --> 20:37.422
But most people who call me that
don't get away with it.

20:37.505 --> 20:41.259
Actually, that guy was the only one
who ever called me a fizzle.

20:41.259 --> 20:46.472
After today, only half the people who called
me a fizzle will have gotten away with it.

20:46.597 --> 20:49.182
A new challenger has entered the field.

20:49.307 --> 20:52.311
The crowd has fallen deathly ill.
Silent. Sorry.

21:06.491 --> 21:08.076
Oh, my God, I'm gonna die!

21:08.994 --> 21:12.664
To the owner of a yellow Hyundai,
your car is being towed.

21:12.747 --> 21:13.791
What?

21:15.375 --> 21:17.335
I won!

21:18.295 --> 21:23.299
- Peter, that was amazing. You were so brave.
- Nice going, Dad.

21:23.382 --> 21:25.593
Boy, that was lucky about the car.

21:25.676 --> 21:29.847
Take that, you bastard! Nobody
makes a fool out of Mort Goldman!

21:30.473 --> 21:35.687
Spectacular, maggot! How'd you like
to travel with us as our lead jouster?

21:35.687 --> 21:38.940
Thanks, but no thanks, Coach.
I've lived my dream.

21:39.023 --> 21:42.150
And besides, my life is here with my family.

21:42.276 --> 21:45.071
But, Mom, what's Dad gonna do for a job?

21:45.071 --> 21:48.533
Lt'll be OK, Chris. Remember
that episode of The Honeymooners

21:48.616 --> 21:51.535
when Ralph lost his job but didn't get it back?

21:51.660 --> 21:54.787
Yeah, why was that?
That bugged the crap out of me.

21:54.788 --> 22:55.788
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru